                    <h3>Combining <span class="accent">what fits</span></h3>
                    <p>
                        Natural compounds are mapped to what they can reach.
                        When two or more hit the same pathway from different
                        angles, they act together — molecular synergy, not
                        single-agent suppression.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Match</strong> each natural compound to the sites it reaches</li>
                        <li><strong>Combine</strong> compounds that converge on the same pathway</li>
                        <li><strong>Reserve</strong> covalent binding for what must stay anchored</li>
                        <li><strong>Refine</strong> a molecule only when nature falls short</li>
                    </ul>
