<section id="different">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Most tools solve <span class="accent">one piece</span>.<br>GAIA runs the whole chain — and then goes further.</h2>

        <div class="movements">

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 Q 8 8 14 20 T 26 20 T 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It reads the genome <em>backward</em>.</h3>
                    <p>Standard pipelines pick a target, then ask which variants matter. GAIA starts from the raw genome and the patient's own symptom pattern, and works back to the genes actually producing the disease. Nothing is hand-coded. Everything is derived.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 L 10 20 L 12 12 L 16 28 L 20 20 L 28 20 L 30 10 L 34 30 L 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="1s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It reawakens what disease <em>silences</em>.</h3>
                    <p>Disease doesn't just damage tissue — it shuts down the repair pathways that would heal it. GAIA identifies compounds that reactivate those silenced signals, the difference between managing a disease and reversing it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 30 L 12 30 L 16 14 L 20 34 L 24 22 L 28 30 L 38 30"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="2s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It <em>reverses</em>, not just manages.</h3>
                    <p>Diseases silence the pathways that would repair them. GAIA finds compounds that reawaken those signals — and the same pathways also repair the DNA damage that accumulates with age. In simulation, a single treatment protocol reverses up to ten years of DNA-repair deficit.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="movement">
                <div class="movement-mark">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="40" height="40">
                        <path d="M 2 20 L 10 20 L 14 10 L 20 30 L 26 10 L 32 30 L 36 20 L 38 20"
                              fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <animate attributeName="stroke-dasharray" values="0 200;200 0" dur="4s" begin="3s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="movement-body">
                    <h3>It <em>checks itself</em> before it speaks.</h3>
                    <p>Every prediction is verified against three independent layers — computational, cellular, physiological. A claim that survives all three is worth acting on. A claim that survives only computation is not a claim. It is a guess.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

